WEBVTT

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.360
A container image is assembled from build instructions and filesystem layers.

00:00:04.580 --> 00:00:08.500
The base image may provide an operating system, a minimal distribution,

00:00:08.720 --> 00:00:10.880
or a language-specific runtime.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:15.660
Later layers add packages, application dependencies, configuration, and code.

00:00:15.880 --> 00:00:17.880
Patch scope begins with those inputs.

00:00:18.100 --> 00:00:20.980
Operating-system packages may be inherited from the base.

00:00:21.200 --> 00:00:25.520
Language runtimes and package managers introduce their own release cycles.

00:00:25.740 --> 00:00:29.580
Application libraries can be installed directly, pulled transitively,

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:31.960
or copied from another build stage.

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:35.300
The container build file defines how the artifact is created.

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.240
Pinning, repository configuration, build stages, copied files,

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:43.900
and cleanup all affect what remains in the final image.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:49.400
Updating a package in one layer does not help if an older vulnerable copy is still present

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:50.420
elsewhere.

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:52.640
Shared ancestry creates fan-out.

00:00:52.860 --> 00:00:56.780
Many teams may build from the same organization base image or dependency set,

00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:00.840
so one vulnerable component can appear in dozens of application images.

00:01:01.060 --> 00:01:05.700
A base-image fix reduces risk only after dependent images are rebuilt, promoted,

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:07.680
and redeployed.

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:12.300
Tags can move, while digests identify exact image content.

00:01:12.520 --> 00:01:17.400
Patch records should connect source revision, base digest, dependency inventory,

00:01:17.620 --> 00:01:22.900
build provenance, image digest, registry location, and deployed workload.

00:01:23.120 --> 00:01:26.080
This chain lets teams prove which version is actually running.

00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:31.020
Minimize image contents and maintain a software bill of materials to make scope visible.

00:01:31.240 --> 00:01:37.080
Removing unused tools and packages reduces both attack surface and remediation workload.

00:01:37.300 --> 00:01:39.780
The objective is not simply a newer tag;

00:01:40.000 --> 00:01:44.320
it is a reproducible image whose vulnerable components were replaced or removed.
